# Copy to .env and fill in the values that exist. .env is gitignored.
#
# Vite exposes ONLY VITE_-prefixed variables to the client bundle. Anything
# with that prefix is compiled into JavaScript that anyone can read, so no
# secret may ever carry it. Server-only values (API keys) have no prefix and
# are read exclusively by api/*.js at runtime.


# ── The production origin ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ONE VARIABLE, ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH. scripts/site-origin.mjs resolves it and
# vite.config.ts injects the result as a compile-time constant, so canonical
# URLs, og:url, JSON-LD, the sitemap and robots.txt cannot disagree.
#
# The default is https://www.trenvomedia.com — set this ONLY to override it,
# which is what a preview deployment should do so it does not advertise itself
# as production.
#
# ⚠ THE DEFAULT IS THE www HOST, AND THAT IS MEASURED, NOT STYLISTIC.
#   Verified 1 September 2026:
#     https://trenvomedia.com/     -> 308 -> https://www.trenvomedia.com/
#     https://www.trenvomedia.com/ -> 200
#   www is the host that answers 200, so it is the canonical origin. Pointing
#   canonical/og:url/sitemap at the apex would make every one of them a URL
#   that redirects.
#
# ⚠ NEVER SET THIS TO AN EMPTY STRING. Production previously had SITE_ORIGIN
#   defined but blank, and the old `??` fallback did not catch it — the site
#   shipped canonical="/", og:url="/" and a sitemap of relative <loc> values,
#   all silently ignored by crawlers. resolveOrigin() now treats blank as
#   unset, but leaving it undefined is cleaner than setting it empty.
#
# SITE_URL=https://preview.trenvomedia.com


# ── Lead delivery (api/contact.js) ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix these with VITE_.
#
# The contact form POSTs to /api/contact, which dispatches to whichever
# provider is configured below. With NEITHER configured the endpoint answers
# 503 `not_configured` and the form falls back to a pre-filled mailto: — so a
# lead is never silently swallowed, but it is also not delivered automatically.
#
# Configure ONE of the two.
#
# Option 1 — email via Resend:
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# LEAD_TO_EMAIL=hello@trenvomedia.com
# LEAD_FROM_EMAIL=Trenvo Media <noreply@trenvomedia.com>
#
# Option 2 — POST the JSON payload anywhere (Zapier, Make, Slack, a CRM):
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.example.com/xxxxx
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_SECRET=shared-secret-sent-as-X-Trenvo-Signature


# ── Analytics (src/lib/analytics.ts) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Cookieless and OFF unless an endpoint is set. No third-party script is ever
# loaded, which is what lets the Content-Security-Policy stay strict — see
# SECURITY-HEADERS.md.
#
# Any collector that accepts a JSON POST works (Plausible, Umami, a Cloudflare
# Worker, an internal service). PUBLIC VALUES ONLY: these are compiled into the
# client bundle.
#
# ⚠ scripts/apply-csp.mjs reads VITE_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT AT BUILD TIME to add its
#   origin to connect-src. If you set this after building, rebuild — otherwise
#   the CSP will block the requests.
#
# VITE_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT=https://analytics.example.com/api/event
# VITE_ANALYTICS_SITE_ID=trenvomedia


# ── Contact endpoint override (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# Defaults to the same-origin /api/contact. Set this only when the lead
# endpoint lives somewhere else — and if you do, add that origin to
# `connect-src` in scripts/apply-csp.mjs, or the browser will block the POST.
#
# VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=https://api.trenvomedia.com/contact
